# Parquet columns are widened at the scan (LANGUAGE.md §5.1): Timestamp(ns) and Date32 to
# `datetime`, Int16 and UInt32 to `long`, Float32 to `real`, a dictionary to `string`, a
# decimal to `real`. Binary has no DataScript type and can only be projected.
mode: check
show: schema
---- query
from '../../data/types.parquet' | take 1;
from '../../data/types.parquet' | where bin == 'x'
---- expected
error[DS2008]: column `bin` has a type DataScript cannot use yet
  --> query:2:41
  |
2 | from '../../data/types.parquet' | where bin == 'x'
  |                                         ^^^ this column is `Binary` in Arrow
  |
  = help: it can only be projected as it is: `project bin`, `project-away bin`
  = note: column `bin` was read from ../../data/types.parquet
  = note: nested, JSON and GUID columns become `dynamic` and `guid` values in M2

query 1 columns:
  id: long
  ts_ns: datetime
  ts_tz: datetime
  date: datetime
  i16: long
  u32: long
  f32: real
  dict: string
  dec: real
  bin: (error)

query 2 columns:
  id: long
  ts_ns: datetime
  ts_tz: datetime
  date: datetime
  i16: long
  u32: long
  f32: real
  dict: string
  dec: real
  bin: (error)
